1. Functional Requirements

a)Create Task: User enters a description. The system automatically assigns a unique ID and
sets the status to PENDING.

b)View All Tasks: Display a formatted table showing ID, Description,
and Status (Pending/Completed).

c)Mark Task as Complete: User enters the Task ID to toggle its status.

d)Delete Task: User enters the Task ID to remove it from the list.

e)Data Persistence: When the app starts, it reads from tasks.txt.
When the user adds/deletes, it saves to tasks.txt. This is the most important "Pro" feature.

2. Technical Requirements (The "Pro" Checklist)

Object-Oriented Design
Generics: Use an ArrayList<Task>

Encapsulation: All fields in your Task class should be private with public getters/setters.

Error Handling: Use try-catch blocks to handle "File Not Found" or when a user types a
letter instead of a Task ID number.

Enum for Status: Instead of using a String for "Pending," use a Java Enum.